Z||000000||Philphine||06-17-2001||11:00 PM||||<BR>i got a set for my '87 and for my chevy and neither set had aiming instructions. i have one set on but aimed pretty low just to be on the safe side (hate being blinded by someone who just threw them on). anyone got a method?||||reg||1
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-17-2001||11:12 PM||||I find the driving lights work the same as regular headlights..  I find a quick & easy way to measure is to park approx. 20 feet from a wall,(garage,house,etc) and turn on your brights..   measure the height from the center of the beam at the headlight to the ground.. and measure the same height on the wall.<P>so if your headlights at the car are 26" off the ground.. measure 26" on the wall and aim the lights there..     <P>I find it works pretty good  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
